OL,3,GNEWSAJudge engaged in sexualised
OL,4,Abehaviour with staff
OL,5,
OL,6,FGaskell, who worked in Birmingham,
OL,7,Fresigned in March while under
OL,8,Finvestigation for his behaviour towards
OL,9,Fwomen he worked alongside. The
OL,10,Finvestigation concluded his actions
OL,11,Famounted to gross misconduct and he
OL,12,Fwould have been sacked if he was still
OL,13,Fa sitting member of the judiciary.
OL,15,FThe Judicial Conduct Investigations
OL,16,FOffice (JCIO) said Gaskell denied the
OL,17,Fallegations and had insisted any
OL,18,Fphysical contact with female staff had
OL,19,Fbeen "inadvertent".
